ementation successfully integrates with the Pydantic schema. Investigating the server component, focusing on the file upload endpoint. The task is to replace the existing invoice upload backend with a FastAPI implementation, integrating the Google GenAI.\n\n\nDefined data models for invoice items and extracted invoices, adhering to a structured format for extracted information. Implemented an API endpoint to handle file uploads and perform invoice analysis using a large language model. The endpoint reads the uploaded file, determines its MIME type, and constructs a prompt with rules for the large language model to extract specific invoice details. The response of the model is formatted to conform to the `ExtractedInvoice` Pydantic model.\n\n\nImplemented CORS middleware to allow API access from any origin. Integrated the `InvoiceItem` and `ExtractedInvoice` Pydantic schemas, and the `/api/analyze-bill` endpoint. Added API key handling, fallback mechanisms for API failures, and integrated the large language model call with data sanitization.\n\nEnsured existing utility endpoints `/api/clean-items` and `/api/process-invoice` are maintained within the FastAPI structure. Configured static file serving to handle the frontend assets. Verified the server will run with Uvicorn, listening on all interfaces, specifying port with helpful error messages if the gemini api key is missing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.staticfiles import StaticFiles\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n\napp = FastAPI()\napp.mount('/', StaticFiles(directory='/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it', html=True), name='static')\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\nr = client.get('/')\nprint('Status code for /:', r.status_code)\nprint('Content type:', r.headers.get('content-type'))\nassert r.status_code == 200\nassert 'AUDIT IT' in r.